        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Allium litardierei is a North African species of wild onion native to Algeria and Morocco."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "The oldest name applied to the taxon is the 1924 moniker Allium paniculatum subsp. breviscapum Litard. & Maire. Elevating the epithet breviscapum to species level is prevented by the existence of the 1885 name Allium breviscapum Stapf, hence the need for a new name, Allium litardierei J.-M.Tison in 2010."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
